{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact explicit-grants head 6f36312a7e4836ba287fcea05aec60d174501478 on builder/explicit-grants-20261104, tree 987fe186, for request 0ca13069 under promise 4511ed3b and review request 28e8d38f. This approval covers the 27 paths at this head. Planner ruling 8dba5555 still governs when the shared checkout may merge it.\n\nScope. Main 7135dc39 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head adds two commits, and the commit-message check passes for both. The paths are test files, test support, two guide paragraphs, the note and two manifests. No production source, configuration, dependency, package export or card path changes. Source commit af21a3f4 has tree 44a7ba38, the gate tree. Only the note and the two manifests change after it.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The guarantee is small and stated in one sentence: a refusal expectation names the check that refused. The mechanism is the existing Vitest matchers plus one method rename. It meets Hugh's bar in ruling d6aa9122.\n- `Ledger` now has `allActionGrants()` as its named broad default and `presentedGrants()` as the provider that `context()` reads. Grow's two per-key assignments and Replay's three overrides move to `presentedGrants`, so their narrower grants still apply. An explicit `context({ grants })` still spreads last and overrides the provider. A search finds no leftover `grants()` override of `Ledger`. The one remaining `override grants()`, in archive-native-authority.ts, belongs to the scope package's own `Lane`, and the gate's typecheck passes.\n- The 64-site baseline holds. classified-assertions.json lists 64 sites in 18 files at tree 17b307e0: 35 bare states, 21 unnamed guards and 8 aggregates. It also lists 5 exclusions with reasons. None of the 64 original expectation lines remains unchanged at this head.\n- The two setup corrections fix real wrong-reason passes. Counter now asks the non-controller while the board is paused, so the controller guard decides. Lending now passes `reason` only to `cancel`, and all three acts refuse with `final`.\n- The paired judge test submits one signed `assign` from the wrong requester twice. With its grant it fails `guards.1`, and without it it fails `unauthorized`. Each matcher is shown to reject the other real answer. This is the distinction the request asks for.\n- The record keeps both compiler failures and the 217-pass, 3-fail first body. It names the three expected checks that source inspection corrected: `bad-field`, `revision-moved` and `guards.3`.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit reads exit 0. All five stages pass: kernel, node, counting, plain and native. The counts are 135 node, 56 counting, 3,912 plain with one skip and 1,078 native with two skips. before.json and after.json record head af21a3f4, tree 44a7ba38, a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43. receipt.json shows exit 0, unchanged source and no owned process left after 1,637.3 seconds.\n\nEvidence. The two manifests list 23 public files. All match their sizes and digests and are read-only, both SHA256SUMS files match, and the note names both manifest digests. The scan finds no credential. All 40 selected gate originals match, the gate's private inventory of 2,277 files matches with no unlisted file, and every file has mode 0400. The six focused private units hold 621 files, and every file matches its unit's SHA256SUMS.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Fixture authority now has a visible name and one override point, and production judges change nothing.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Tests that refuse for authorization reasons must now say `unauthorized`, so a missing grant can no longer pass as a business guard.\n\nSimplification: no required change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cd898b40a75e18dc13e4c6e17f55c40625ac69dc","binding":"assigned","head":"6f36312a7e4836ba287fcea05aec60d174501478","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4d1c546bf8442459d5f001bc841491